SPOSITIF A SEMI-CONDUCTEURS</invention-title><citations><patent-citations><patcit ucid="JP-10200001-A" status="new"><document-id status="new" format="epo"><country>JP</country><doc-number>10200001</doc-number><kind>A</kind></document-id><sources><source category="X" name="SEA"  created-by-npl="N"/></sources></patcit><patcit ucid="JP-2054572-A" status="new"><document-id status="new" format="epo"><country>JP</country><doc-number>2054572</doc-number><kind>A</kind></document-id><sources><source category="X" name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></patcit><patcit ucid="JP-63004671-A"  status="new"><document-id status="new"  format="epo"><country>JP</country> <doc-number>63004671</doc-number><kind>A</kind></document-id><sources><source category="X"  name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></patcit> <patcit ucid="US-5798965-A" status="new"><document-id status="new" format="epo"><country>US</country> <doc-number>5798965</doc-number> <kind>A</kind></document-id><sources><source category="X" name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></patcit></patent-citations></citations></technical-data><parties><applicants><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>HITACHI EUROP LTD</name><address><country>GB</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>HITACHI LTD</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>ITO KIYOO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>NAKAZATO KAZUO</name><address><country>GB</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>HITACHI EUROPE LIMITED</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>HITACHI, LTD.</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>ITO, KIYOO</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>NAKAZATO, KAZUO</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>ITO KIYOO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>NAKAZATO KAZUO</name><address><country>GB</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>ITO, KIYOO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>NAKAZATO, KAZUO</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>The operation of conventional large-capacity DRAMs (dynamic random access memories) is liable to be unstable because the read signal voltage of memory cell is low. If the signal voltage is raised by imparting an enough gain to memory cells, the memory cell area, in turn, increases. Therefore it has been desired that a memory cell operating stable, having a small area, and capable of operating as a RAM is available. A memory cell of the invention has, for example, a three-dimensional structure including a MOS transistor for holding information voltage, a write transistor (e.g. tunneling transistor) for supplying the information voltage, and a capacitor for controlling the voltage of the gate, thereby realizing a high-speed stably-operating semiconductor device of low cost. The semiconductor device can have a nonvolatile RAM function.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>Le fonctionnement de mémoires vives dynamiques (D-RAM) classiques à grande capacité est menacé d'instabilité dans la mesure où la tension de signal de lecture de la mémoire est basse. Si l'on élève cette tension de signal de lecture en affectant un gain suffisant aux cellules mémoire, la surface de cellule mémoire augmente également. Il est donc souhaitable de disposer d'une cellule mémoire à fonctionnement stable, de petite surface et capable de fonctionner comme mémoire vive. La cellule mémoire selon l'invention possède, par exemple, une structure tridimensionnelle comportant un transistor MOS destiné à maintenir la tension d'information, un transistor pour la fonction d'écriture (par ex. un transistor à effet tunnel) fournissant la tension d'information et un condensateur agissant sur la tension de la grille, ce qui permet d'obtenir un dispositif à semi-conducteurs à fonctionnement stable et à vitesse élevée et, de plus, d'un faible coût. Ce dispositif à semi-conducteurs est doté d'une fonction de mémoire vive rémanente.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>